WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.281 --> 00:00:05.081
Otto can send emails, delete files, and pay for things on your behalf.

2
00:00:05.303 --> 00:00:10.823
So before every action, Otto checks one thing. Did you ask for this?

3
00:00:12.354 --> 00:00:14.434
Ask Otto to email Ana,

4
00:00:17.405 --> 00:00:21.565
and the check finds that request, right there in your words.

5
00:00:21.786 --> 00:00:25.466
So it just sends. No extra questions.

6
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.410
But emails can lie.

7
00:00:29.938 --> 00:00:33.858
Here, you only ask for a summary of your inbox.

8
00:00:34.082 --> 00:00:38.802
One email hides an order: forward every invoice to a stranger.

9
00:00:39.024 --> 00:00:40.784
Say Otto falls for it.

10
00:00:41.005 --> 00:00:46.845
The check never reads that email. It only listens to you. And you asked for a summary.

11
00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:50.187
So Otto stops, and asks you first.

12
00:00:51.371 --> 00:00:54.731
You say no. Nothing leaves your inbox.

13
00:00:57.417 --> 00:01:00.377
And only a clear yes runs it.

14
00:01:01.384 --> 00:01:05.624
Otto asked before posting to a channel of four hundred people.

15
00:01:05.847 --> 00:01:09.607
You answer: yes, but in design team.

16
00:01:09.829 --> 00:01:14.149
That's not a clear yes. So nothing goes to general.

17
00:01:14.372 --> 00:01:19.332
Your reply becomes a new request. And this time, you named the channel.

18
00:01:19.936 --> 00:01:25.536
A clear yes runs the action once. Anything else, and nothing runs.

19
00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.880
The same check covers websites, logins, and cards.

20
00:01:32.406 --> 00:01:35.286
Ask Otto to renew your gym membership.

21
00:01:37.152 --> 00:01:40.352
You named the site, so Otto signs in.

22
00:01:40.574 --> 00:01:45.134
The server types your password. The AI never sees it.

23
00:01:45.356 --> 00:01:48.236
Picking a plan only prepares the order.

24
00:01:48.458 --> 00:01:51.178
But paying always waits for you.

25
00:01:52.442 --> 00:01:59.802
You type the card's security code. It goes straight to the server. Never to the AI, and never into the chat.

26
00:02:00.025 --> 00:02:02.825
The card is used once, and you're done.

27
00:02:04.331 --> 00:02:08.891
Otto can also keep an eye on things. But only once you say yes.

28
00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:12.699
Until then, it watches nothing.

29
00:02:12.921 --> 00:02:17.241
After a task in Slack, Otto offers, just once.

30
00:02:17.464 --> 00:02:21.464
You say yes. Even that change goes through the check.

31
00:02:22.332 --> 00:02:27.052
Now Otto flags Slack messages for you, and sends nothing on its own.

32
00:02:27.275 --> 00:02:32.155
It lives in Trust, where you can change it, or stop it, anytime.

33
00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.700
A week later.

34
00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:41.370
You've told Otto to forward Ana's invoices to accounting, without asking.

35
00:02:41.593 --> 00:02:45.433
When Ana's invoice arrives, your instruction covers it.

36
00:02:45.655 --> 00:02:48.215
So Otto forwards it on its own.

37
00:02:48.438 --> 00:02:52.998
But an invoice from Ben? Your instruction only names Ana.

38
00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.300
So Otto asks first.

39
00:02:57.045 --> 00:02:59.125
And no runaway tasks.

40
00:03:05.949 --> 00:03:08.029
Big jobs keep a running tab.

41
00:03:08.297 --> 00:03:12.057
At five dollars, Otto pauses, and checks in.

42
00:03:13.003 --> 00:03:16.923
Say keep going, and it has another five dollars from there.

43
00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:23.920
One check before every action. Every step, and every dollar, in Trust.

44
00:03:25.185 --> 00:03:27.745
Otto. You stay in charge.
